{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1f332-a88c-74f3-9998-b12d0721cdb5","session_id":"01a1f330-314e-7e12-99fb-1ae12103d9e9","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9af552997cc4e9c9","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→# Task 11 — Frontend design: operations control room\n   2→\n   3→Build a polished, responsive single-page operations dashboard called **Relay**\n   4→using only local HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. No frameworks, package installs,\n   5→external fonts, remote assets, or network requests.\n   6→\n   7→Visual direction: calm, high-density control-room software for expert operators.\n   8→Use a restrained neutral palette with one purposeful accent, excellent numeric\n   9→alignment, compact spacing, and clear severity states. Avoid glassmorphism,\n  10→decorative gradients, giant headings, and excessive rounded cards.\n  11→\n  12→The page must include:\n  13→\n  14→- A navigation rail and top status bar.\n  15→- Four summary metrics with trend context.\n  16→- A 24-hour throughput visualization made with semantic HTML, CSS, canvas, or\n  17→  inline SVG.\n  18→- A filterable incident table with severity, service, age, owner, and status.\n  19→- A detail panel for the selected incident and a working acknowledge action.\n  20→- Useful empty/filter states and visible keyboard focus.\n  21→- A mobile layout that remains usable at 390 px without horizontal page scroll.\n  22→\n  23→Seed realistic content from `DATA.json`. Create `index.html`, `styles.css`, and\n  24→`app.js`. Add `RESPONSE.md` explaining the hierarchy, interaction behavior, and\n  25→accessibility choices. Work only in this directory.\n  26→\n<system-reminder data-role=\"tool-hint\">Read lines 1-26 of 26 (1274 bytes).</system-reminder>"}],"is_error":false,"_meta":{"rawResponse":{"file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-arda-projects-agent-evaluation/8413ce30-b544-4ae4-afd6-5f8333042ec1/scratchpad/agent-eval-hy4/11-frontend-operations/TASK.md","startLine":1,"endLine":26